      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "UTAH JAZZ NZ (3) is a newcomer to the Jason Grimson yard from NZ where she has been tackling good company this campaign, highlighted by a fresh win at Listed level three back at Addington. Proven at the distance and the good draw gives her every chance to make an immediate impact. LUX AETERNA (9) is a quality mare who overcame this same barrier at Redcliffe last time, racing parked before getting home by 5m. Owns a decent record at this circuit and distance and can never be ruled out when tackling her own sex. ISLA ROCHELLE (2) made it three seconds on the trot when she led and boxed on behind LUX AETERNA last week. Draws to give a sight again. Big step up in grade for TILLY JAYNE (11) but she has been racing well.",
